+| POST | `/projects/{pid}/members/{uid}/move` | `{"toProjectId"}` → 200 `{"userId","projectId","role"}` |
+
+Moving a member removes them from `{pid}` and adds them to `toProjectId` with
+the same role. The caller must be a manager of both projects (403), neither may
+be archived (409), the user must be a member of `{pid}` (404), must not already
+be a member of the target (409), and the target must differ from `{pid}` (400)
+and be readable by the caller (404). Tasks of `{pid}` assigned to the moved
+user become unassigned, so an assignee stays a member of the task's project.
 
 Statuses: `open`, `doing`, `done`. Errors are `{"error":"..."}`. Request
 bodies are JSON (`Content-Type: application/json`).
